        {
          "explanation": {
            "content": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "All the oxygen atoms have lone pairs that could be donated to a metal ion. However, oxalate can only approach a metal from one side, so only two oxygen atoms will bond to the metal atom. Oxalate is a bidentate ligand."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "448718754",
                "type": "p"
              }
